Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:45:21 +0800
Subject: media: platform: add the HiSTB VPSS video processing driver

The block sits between a decoder and an encoder or a display and has no
mainline driver.
Only tone mapping, temporal noise reduction, a second output port and a
write-back capture channel have no V4L2 mem2mem shape, so they stay
unimplemented.
Add the driver as a mem2mem device: the probe path, the two queues, the
register layer and the job path, the horizontal and vertical flips, the
payload and timestamp of the frame actually written, the crop taken from
the selection API and the scaler driven by the block's own phase tables.
An interlaced field is bobbed into a frame through the pre-scaler's
field filter while the capture rectangle is twice its height, and any
other interlaced combination is refused with a warning instead of
silently converting; the buffers a stopped queue still holds come back
at stop_streaming.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
